      "text": "Field of blood. The popular name for the field bought with the money returned to the chief priests by Judas (Matt. 27:3–10). From Acts 1:18–19 it appears to have been so called as being the scene of his death. It was afterwards used as a buryingplace for “strangers” (Jews of the dispersion and proselytes).",
